First of all, that ant's acting funny.  Soldier ants get two attacks
per round, and the *second* attack is poisoned.  This one got in six
attacks, or three rounds of two each, but the *first* attack of the
second round was poisoned.  That just ain't right.

Second, that unicorn's also acting odd.  It's hard to get a unicorn
into your line of fire even when you're fast--their AI intentionally
avoids getting into a direct line-of-fire with the player.  And yet
this poor Valk, intrinsically slow, tangled up in a spider web, managed
to kill the unicorn with a pair of thrown daggers...

...which were also acting really, really odd.  That corpse isn't on a
line of fire with the player.  So either the player managed to find the
only daggers in the game capable of killing on something *other* than
the eight "normal" directions, the unicorn died off the visible map
area, or the player is no longer standing on the spider web (which
would then have to be off screen, and we'd have no way to guess how
many moves we have left before the food poisoning gets us).  If either
of these last two are the case, the player is, most likely, screwed.
If the first option is the case, then we're playing a hacked version of
the game, and nothing's predictable--that unicorn may not have even
dropped a horn.

You can't win this scenario, because you either don't have enough
information, or it's impossible to get into this scenario in the first
place.

